    "abstract": "Parts breakdown of the forward cargo door surround corner region, showing the four corner fittings in both the aluminium-lithium and the titanium standard against the retained frame web assembly.",
    "sections": {
      "purpose": "This figure gives the parts breakdown of the forward cargo door surround corner region, from the frame web assembly outward to the four corner fittings and their attaching hardware.",
      "figure_note": "Sheet 1 shows the left-hand side looking outboard; the right-hand side is symmetrically opposite and is not drawn separately. Sheet 2 shows the fastener pattern at the lower forward corner. Items 20 and 20A are the two corner fitting standards and must not be mixed on one door surround: the fastener patterns differ and the frame is drilled to one or the other. The attachment set follows the fitting, not the aircraft: items 30 and 40 are ordered against a fitting at item 20, items 30A and 40A against a fitting at item 20A. The countersunk washer at item 40A is not a substitute for the plain washer at item 40 and the two are not interchangeable in either direction."
    },
